  "description": "One More Light is the seventh studio album by American rock band Linkin Park. It was released on May 19, 2017, through Warner Bros. Records and Machine Shop. It is the band's first album to have a title track, as they felt that the song \"One More Light\" was the heart of the album. It is also the band's final album to feature two of their longtime members: co-lead vocalist Chester Bennington, who died by suicide two months after the album's release, and drummer and co-founder Rob Bourdon, who opted not to return for the band's reformation in 2024.",
